    additionalSections:[{id:"spacecraft",title:"Spacecraft work after 1985",html:"<p>Boeing competes for both government and company-funded spacecraft work after private orbital procurement expands. Its recognized industrial strengths include large transports, heavy orbital structures, freight systems, long-endurance vehicles, and integration of complete vehicle systems.</p><p>The archive does not yet identify a complete Boeing commercial catalog or assign particular O-Hundred spacecraft, orbital yards, or carrier fleets to the company. Manufacturer project numbers become important in the period, but Boeing's setting-specific numbering sequence remains open.</p>"}],
