    formation:"<p>In the working post-divergence company history, Consolidated combines with Vultee to form Convair. San Diego and Fort Worth serve as major centers, but the legal sequence, facilities, and organizational form remain incorporated or open.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p>",
    war:"<p>Consolidated's Model 28 became the PBY Catalina and Model 32 the B-24 Liberator before divergence. These programs supply inherited long-range airframe and production experience.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='p'>[p]</sup></p>",
    postwar:"<p>In the working register, F-102 and F-106 form an operational delta-interceptor line, and Convair Model 4 becomes B-58A. Its four engines, delta wing, crew, pod, 1959 introduction, and high-supersonic strategic role are incorporated reconstruction.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p>",
